/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:57:''What the shape answers.'' The `lares` and `lararium` documents live in one place, the Kahu realm of the Nexus whose cabal writes them; on a lone hearth that realm belongs to its operator, who stands as its own Kahu. Every other vessel holds their snapshots by CID. A vessel's own pointers rest in its own bootstrap, so no shared document hosts another vessel's url and nothing merges across siblings. A wiki's floor moves only on a person's accept of a signed release, face by face, so one vessel may hold two Nexuses' floors and ties no face to another.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:65:* ''The shared document merges siblings' pointers.'' `oracleGenesisDocUrl()` gives every vessel one id, and each vessel writes its own `lares` and `lararium` urls, crossroads pin and realm pointers into it (`genesis-artifact.ts` `mintLaresIfAbsent`, `who-face.ts`, `realm-plane.ts`). Two vessels that each mint their own `lares` document settle on ONE `LARES_DOC_URI` once they sync; the control, never connected, keeps each its own (`packages/lararium-node/tests/shared-oracle-doc.probe.test.ts`, on lane `--w26-floor-1`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:67:* ''One signed floor object stands, and it names no Nexus.'' `OraclePointer` (domain `oracle-pointer`) signs a cid, heads and parents under the vessel seed (`oracle-substrate.ts`, `mountOracleReadFace`); readers pin the hearth's key.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:76:# ''The floor.'' A manifest CID names history-free snapshots of the `lares` and `lararium` rows beside the engine CIDs; `@oracle` mounts as its read-face, read-only, under every recipe; genesis bakes the first floor, its corpus CID in the seed, in one labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE`. Red: a minted wiki reads a system carrier through `@oracle` and its write refuses.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:77:# ''Pointers go home.'' Each vessel's own document pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap; the shared `@oracle` document as a writable registry retires. `shared-oracle-doc.probe` (`packages/lararium-node/tests/shared-oracle-doc.probe.test.ts`) turns into this slice's red: two synced vessels each keep their own pointer. `W21` re-cuts here: a joinee mounts its hearth's floor by CID.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:79:# ''The release answer.'' One porch body per Nexus, sealed by the steward under its own signing domain, `floor-release` (operator-approved, 2026-10-18), the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes attached; the crossroads board carries it; `P8` folds in. `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN` retires once releases stand.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:80:# ''The accept act.'' A person's act moves a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) to a newer release that verifies against that Nexus's charter at its epoch and links to the pinned release; no clock and no automatic accept. With no Nexus speaking, a face stands on its last accepted floor, or genesis.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:98:''THE LINEAGE RIDES THE RECORD, NEVER THE CARD.'' The release record and the porch answer carry the charter's epoch lineage, so a herm and a browser verify a release holding the Nexus AID alone. A card holds 4096 characters and the lineage self-certifies against the AID, so the card stays small. The carrier changes nothing about trust: the AID that anchors the lineage comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins, never from the same answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`foreign-nexus`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:118:* RETIRED at slice 4: `OraclePointer`, `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN`, `snapshotPublicOracle` and the node's oracle floor serve. The floor answers by the release at the porch; the flow map keeps its own pointer under `FLOW_POINTER_DOMAIN` (`flow-pointer`), and `oracle-substrate`, `oracle-read-client` and `oracle-read-face` live on as `flow-substrate`, `flow-read-client` and `flow-read-face`. Left for an o-takiage pass: the route and gate names that still say "oracle" (`ORACLE_SOCKET_ROUTE`, `OracleFloorGate`, `OracleGateArgs`), which name the flow map's socket and not a pointer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:119:* Canon lines that named "the shared floor CID" now describe the release (`oracle-governance#/board-model`, `pronaos#/the-rung-ladder`, `genesis-doc#/the-oracle-pointer`, `disk-projection`, `dreamnet-architecture`); the docblocks that call the oracle "the vessel's own plane" or libraries "read-only from wiki" follow the slice whose code makes each line true.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:129:* ''The `bags/oracle` → floor rename'' (the o-takiage left it by ruling). The genesis island document still carries the name `oracle` (`BAG_IDS.oracle`, `ORACLE_BAG`, `oracleUrl`, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/oracle`, the `oracle` plane and recipe-uri segment, the `kind: "oracle"` row tag) because it is the floor's read-face layer under every wiki recipe. It renames together with the layer change that mounts the floor by the accepted pin (slice 5) and the genesis re-bake; `lararium-mesh/tests/o-takiage-names.test.ts` allowlists each such name with this row as its reason, so the list burns down with that lane.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:130:* ''The carriers that still say oracle.'' `lararium/mesh/oracle-governance` (a governance design whose live lines now name the floor release and the flow pointer) and the carrier URIs cited widely keep their names; renaming a carrier moves every citation, so it rides its own lane. `api/pono/oracle` names the oracle sigil (divination), a different sense that stays.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:134:* ''The floor card's freshness.'' The browser verifies the lineage, the head release and the floor bytes from the Nexus AID alone (`browser-floor-read`). The AID rides the same-origin trust line, and the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:143:* ''Branch'': `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--w26-floor-<n>`, one per slice or burst, cut from the span's head. Nothing lands on the span directly.
