/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/l-prime.mem:46:''The basin's true name.'' The ward guards against ''identity-predication (individual-level predication)'' — map fused to territory; the English copula marks its commonest local symptom, not its boundary. ''Transposition law (Perec).'' The discipline transposes across languages by ''function, never by token'': in each tongue it targets that tongue's identity-predication constructions, so a zero-copula grammar satisfies the letter for free while the basin still binds (175/386 languages drop the copula, yet essence/state reroutes everywhere — Pred-heads, case morphology, definiteness). The `${copula}` token-count and the quote-tally serve as the ''English instrument'' of a language-general discipline. Field grounds: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/research-streams/ward-channel-grounds#/ward-basin`.
