/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-law-of-5s.mem:197:''The fold.'' Several strict, best-first rankings over the SAME named items yield one reproducible order. Each ranking names every item exactly once; an absent or repeated item stops the fold rather than inviting a guessed position. The first ranking supplies the stable tie order.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/the-law-of-5s.mem:199:''Two readings.'' Borda adds each item's zero-based positions and advances the lowest sum, a tied sum following the first ranking's order (`bordaConsensus`). Kemeny searches the permutations for the order with the least total Kendall-tau pair disagreement (`kemenyConsensus`, `kendallTauCost`); seeded with Borda and keeping the first equal-cost order, its disagreement never exceeds Borda's. Exhaustive search reaches at most eight items (`KEMENY_MAX_ITEMS`); a larger set takes another method or a refusal, never an unbounded silent search (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/rank-consensus.ts`).
