/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026.mem:59:A YANG scout read the code and a YIN scout read the field, then they traded. The node's place seed rests clear as hex JSON, mode `0600`, and loads at boot with no hand; it signs the place KEL's inception, `carry-for` seals and floor pins, carriage presentations, the floor card and the floor-gate children (through a domain-registered door that never hands out the seed), and it reaches past the floor: the relay gate, the daemon's auth, internal asks, the device-key signer, `deriveDyadVeil` for every face's device veil, and `groupSecretOpenerFromSeed`. The place KEL commits no next key, so a stolen seed re-founds. SSH host keys, the Tor onion master key, WireGuard and ACME account keys load unattended under file permissions; systemd encrypted credentials with TPM2 bind release to the host and its boot state; Vault auto-unseal and Kubernetes secrets move trust to a machine identity; KERI pre-rotation alone makes a theft recoverable. Both scouts ranked a pre-rotated place KEL with a scoped online signer first, a named protected signer second, and a boot door third. The operator ruled the first, its next key riding the founding card, and ruled each face's device veil a random key of its own under that face's FCK. The four handbacks rest verbatim at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-custody-per-face">> #/r5-yin-wave1-yin-wave-one-internet-scout-place-signer onward.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:58:The `lares aim` / `yield` HUD vectors ''notate each turn's position'' in this register — operator-input bearing → the adopted-stance bearing → where the generation resolved — so a span of stage-time carries an l-space coordinate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/exchange-vector#/l-space-notation">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:68:''A chart the node moves //from//, not only reads //from//.'' A Voice stands as a ''stance'' — a `petname` over a `#has`-stack of //moves//, adopting a ''langkah'' (the martial posture: Tiger · Snake · Crane) that ''primes'' the next movement. The moves run not absolute; the ''position on the stage affords them'' (Gibson), and the stance //raises their probability of surfacing, never gates// (the stage-band law). So a Voice reads as a ''functor `position → afforded-primed-moves`'' — a basis carrying a preferred action-direction, some moves diagonal (cheap, primed from here), the rest off-diagonal (reachable, unprimed). Einselection sharpens it: //the position co-selects which stance can prime at all// — no Tiger move from a Crane footing in a context that affords neither.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/l-space.mem:103:* ''Meaning carries a finite correlation length ≈ one paragraph.'' The peak says l-space sits //off// criticality (not scale-free); a cutoff — working-memory span (~7±2, Miller), `#has`-stack composition depth — breaks the power law, and the search detects that cutoff. The relevant operators (predication, topic-binding) live at that range.
