/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:184:* ''Removal's reach'': four edges take a marker (dyad, vouch, member, carriage). A vouch edge answers to its voucher and to a chartered quorum; a seal roll carries every shadow; a standing shadow reaches every gate and drives a key roll; a contested tie keeps the shadow up; mutual removal ends in an explicit fork (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:188:* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:195:* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:204:* ''A cabal shares through the faces its members choose'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18, on the Teshima Family Council story). Kalani founds a private family council; Leilani, already standing on the DreamNet with several faces, chooses which of them join it, and a face she keeps back never learns the council exists. The council's hive reads as a Keyhive group with no key of its own: its members act through their own faces' identities, so nothing stands above them, and a presentation reads valid against the current set without naming which member made it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes">> #/the-handle-chain). Any current member's face promotes into the council's canon; a graft takes the threshold; a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` at the threshold or a fork that omits the captor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">> #/the-unswept-corner); members read the owner-set as faces, never as humans. A private council declares no heraldry and lives in its members' address books under pet-names (cabal-realm #/heraldry). Row `K16` carries the story as `K15`'s acceptance.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:205:* ''The asker seals'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, F6's custody fork). Once the browser holder owns the Repo and the daemon kernel, it routes each sealed write to the admitted tab whose session caused it, else to any admitted, unlocked tab of that write's face; with no awake admitted tab, the write waits, named `seal-awaits-session`, never silent and never decided by a clock. No key material leaves a tab, and each sealer holds the row-class key the occupied carrier's overwrite proof opens. A SharedWorker carries no promise to run while its tabs freeze, and no `MessagePort` event reports a peer's death (round one, 2026-10-19), so a seal that waits names its wait.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:207:* ''A shared act never makes a shared secret'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; four ratcheted research rounds, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">>). Every act that touches more than one face sorts one of three ways: its private bytes DISSOLVE into the owning face's rows (D), its public bytes stand at the FLOOR by design (F), or it names a vessel SECRET (S) whose principal and opener the house names row by row. A mixed carrier splits before it sorts. The browser holds no vessel key: founding, fleet join, slot changes, roster, archives, handle book, dyads, restore and clear sort D or F, so each tab asks only its own face's unlock and public floor work asks nothing. Phones, installed web apps, probes, the CLI, MCP and watcher seats and a native shell hold no S. A tablet waking floor carries ciphertext and public rows unattended and decrypts no face's row. A container restarts at its floor and nothing unlocks it unattended. A guest island that owns a key store stands as its own vessel. A node holds S only for rows it names: the serving key has no row yet, so it guards nothing today. * ''The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; a fifth research round, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">> #/the-place-signer). A node's place identity keeps a KEL whose inception commits the next key, and that next key rides the founding card beside the seed charter's cold next key, offline; the online place signer runs unattended for an enumerated allowlist of floor duties alone (the KEL's own events excepted, which the card's key signs), rests under the host's TPM-bound credential where the host offers one and an owner-only file elsewhere, and never rides an environment, an image or a log. A stolen online signer rotates away by the card; a lost card beside a stolen signer re-founds. The floor holds no custody key; it holds its own named place signer. The format change rides the founding bake (`X0`). Today the place KEL commits no next key and the seed reaches past the floor (`vessel-kel.ts`; `node-vessel-identity.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:227:* ''The fork-resolve act'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A fork stays a fork, and every reader names the branch it follows; no clock, no longest chain and no third-party quorum picks a branch. Two acts resolve one. ABANDON: a seal record a branch's own quorum signs at its head, closing that branch for every reader who holds it, erasing nothing and touching no sibling. REUNION: one canonical image naming the scope AID, both held heads sorted, and the new seats, threshold and successor commitments, signed by each branch's quorum at its head over identical bytes; the verifier proves both heads inside the same AID's lineages from a common ancestor, and the record becomes the common head. A seal record's predecessors form a sorted set of one or two, built before the fence; until the reunion verifier lands, a two-predecessor record refuses `REUNION_UNBUILT`. The reason: a split household reunites only by a paper both halves sign. The ruling flips on a fork that neither branch's quorum can still sign for.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:237:* ''The admit's gate pin'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The admit carriage and fleet-join answer sign a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at the named Nexus, read by `readGateBundlePin`; its digest derives from that object. Dials index by (hearth, Nexus, route, tier). Floor routes receive their own full pins through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set; an announcement never authenticates its own first pin. The reason: a digest alone gives an offline dialer no trusted route or key. The ruling flips on an equally authenticated digest-to-full-pin carrier with an unambiguous route and offline first contact.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:249:* ''The place signer's fifth duty'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean). A place's finish at another place's gate, `GATE_PLACE_FINISH_DOMAIN`, joins the place signer's floor duties: a faceless place that reads another's floor performs a floor act. Each of the five duties binds its domain by an exact head at byte zero, in one table beside the allowlist; `X0` moves the framing into the signer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:251:* ''Sync carries; verification decides'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">> and the controller's leans). A mutable CRDT carries identity claims and never decides them. Each face holds, on each device, a ''sealed identity anchor'' in its own custody (a D row): its PersonaGroup, its persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its device edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Only founding, admission and the recovery rites (guardian rotation, bundle restore, root cards) write an anchor; sync never writes one. Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed records in the face's `@persona` plane, a signed-entry log every reader verifies against the anchor and the KEL; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner. The face planes hold verified projections. A device reads freely; an act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) checks the sealed frontier and refuses a target that names a newer bound, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under. Transparency and witnesses for equivocation wait for their own row. Wave C carries the build inside `K15` step 6.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:252:* ''Wave B's forks'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). A fresh PersonaGroup mints a fresh atom, never an orphan's seed. A tab reads its face's pins from its custody anchor before it opens its session, so the tab's own Repo retires; and each face holds its own social planes in the browser, keyed by PersonaGroup as on the node. Both ride Wave C with the anchor.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:254:* ''The order of the next waves'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). Wave C (`K15` step 6 under the identity anchor) runs next, with `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 beside it on the floor's own ground, their composer hunks passing to the controller as patches, and slice 5 after it, since its accepted floor rests as a face's sealed row (a D row under the face's own FCK once Wave C lands); `I1` follows the anchor; the far agent's relay seat takes its own research after `I1`; `G37`'s renames ride `X0`'s bake; the sensorium resumes after `X0`, on the operator's word.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:332:* ''No keyring stands'' (operator ruling, #/rulings): the code holds no per-Nexus convergence secret. No custody row, seat mint, admission delivery or charter commitment carries one, and a persona admission's signed transcript names no keyring digest. A private body seals under its bag's content key, which reaches its readers through a lockbox (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/keys">>). A seat's act and a roll mint nothing beside the charter epoch. The same ruling's standing law binds every later slice: let a counter, wherever one appears, order one writer's own emissions only; keep the face at the session capability; keep every verified fork head visible; retain by causal evidence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:341:* ''The gate's two root doors'' (specified in code; no composer calls them until the socket cutover): a floor gate's bundle derives through the floor key's door, which answers at a locked vessel, hands back a fresh child and never the floor key (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`); a sovereign gate's bundle derives through the custody seat's door, which answers only while the seat holds its key (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`). The doors carry two types, so no line swaps them by accident; a root refuses the other tier's door by name; each seat's door refuses the other tier's child; and a weld holds the two mints to the two seats (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:363:''R-CHARTER, the one AID train.'' Its first stage stands landed (train K of #/the-trains): the chairs sign with seat keys of their own and pre-rotate on cold cards, a Nexus answers to `nexus-<sha>`, the floor key commits no next key, per-Nexus keys mint at random, the PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act founds a hearth (`lares vessel found --hearth`): the place, persona zero and a PRIVATE seed charter at one seat, with no keyring, every fleet relation bound to that charter's AID, and every harness that founds a hearth founding through it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/found">>). What stays owed:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:369:* A per-Nexus wire key in two tiers (operator ruling): a floor route's bundle derives from the floor key and answers at a locked vessel; a sovereign route's bundle derives from the sealed custody root and stands only while the vessel stands unlocked. One gate per (Nexus, route), so knock, pin, verdict and posture read per Nexus exactly (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). The serving route's third tier rides train E (`E3`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:406:* ''Mutual removal'' (operator ruling; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae">>): both signed acts and both key branches stay, every member sees the conflict, and it ends in an explicit fork unless the realm's charter named a recovery council.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:451:* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) runs next.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:476:* The crossing record's production membrane around the agent worldline (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/mandate-activity-provenance">>); its two forks read in #/open.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:485:* `P9` The re-seal proof and the fork-resolve act stand ruled (#/rulings): the re-seal record builds with sealed-store step three, the fork-resolve act in train N.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:536:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:538:* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; until then each of the five floor duties binds its domain by an exact head matcher), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:604:* `X0b` The idempotent-by-intent pass, after the founding bake, paralleling the isomorphic-by-intent law (operator, 2026-10-19): a replay, a reboot and a retry land nothing new. Every row names itself by its content or its causal id, never a clock or a counter; every write reads first-writer-wins or merges by its CRDT; every boot reads as a function of its stores; and every multi-step act either completes or re-enters to the same end. Its instrument: N boots, each Archive replayed twice, each verb retried, and the second pass of each adds no head and no row. Each finding before the bake cures as its own bug; its instrument runs once before the bake as a census beside `G37`, so a finding that renames a persisted row lands inside the bake, and this pass sweeps what remains. X.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:631:* ''The bake's critical path in the operator's hands'' (`X0`). Once strides 1 to 3 stand built, these gate the ceremony and no lane can supply them: guardian count and threshold (`K18`, #/open); the domain and its two credential files (`A2`); one run on the real LAN (`A4`); the device measures (`B3`); the second machine and its operator for the fresh start (`X3`). The operator gathers them at their own pace; none blocks a lane today.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:701:# The floor key commits no next key (`230907f66`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:860:# ''Removal's reach.'' The model stands ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). Five questions stay the operator's, each with the house's lean. Whether an edge act may ever use the emergency class (lean: never). Whether a seated member under a member shadow keeps a seat's signature until the next roll (lean: yes, a seat leaves by a roll alone). What a recovery council holds after a mutual removal (lean: nothing built; the fork stands as the one exit). Whether a holder's key reads at its log's current head, so a recovered face keeps its edges (lean: yes, owed with the resolver of #/side-lanes). Whether a counted raise moves the keys while a lift still races it (lean: yes, remove-wins reaches the keys, and a lift then seats afresh). Two more came with the key side. What removes a seat no standing hand can revoke, the founding vessel's own among them (lean: a fresh group, at the re-founding that moves the PersonaGroup to a Keyhive group). Whether a vessel that holds no revoke authority goes on trying a raise until it sees the seat leave (lean: yes, and each try hands the roll on again, so the content key rolls whoever revokes the seat).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:871:# ''The confirm door upstream.'' The fork asks its questions through the wiki itself (`$tw.utils.confirm`, `tm-confirm`). Owed before a donation: the order of actions after a confirm, a switch for a blocking prompt, and one squashed change. The withdrawn render boundary's upstream pull request, if it still stands open, advertises a design the fork backed out.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem:121:''The interim cure stays out.'' The lane's recipe-watch hold (`--w26-own-canon`, commit `d1983aa75`) keeps a system wiki's own canon against a shared pointer that slice 2 removes; under //build the end state// it lands nowhere. Its probes stand: the shared-oracle probe as slice 2's red, the `W25` creator probe as that row's measurement.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:52:''The face's lineage re-issues the face proof key.'' The standing key and a successor minted at random both sign one hand-over; the record rides the Nexus's carriage board, the admit keeps naming the key the Nexus admitted, and a gate reads that key's line, stands a presenter under its head alone, and reads a line that forks as denied. A kapae on any key of the line holds the whole line. A gate that has not yet read the hand-over still stands the key it handed on, and no shared moment closes that gap; a compromise of the key therefore takes the face-key roll (#/causal-withdrawal), never a hand-over. A Handle card names its handle-KEL prefix, which no per-Nexus key enters, so a hand-over moves no card (house reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:86:# ''The gate checks, still provisionally.'' It checks the pinned route and audience, the chain, the presentation's signatures, the quorum's signatures, the causal parents, the deny events and withdrawals it has learned (#/causal-withdrawal), and the roll anchors. Where the asked planes need it, the ring checks the PersonaGroup grant. Missing required history, a known fork or an incomplete board brings abstention. The gate reveals no differentiated refusal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:101:* ''An OPEN gate answers a stranger.'' A sound chain under a face no quorum admitted, presenting no arm, sorts as a stranger where this Nexus reads OPEN: the gate answers `verified`, seats it at the public shelf and keeps nothing of that face's history. Where the Nexus reads PRIVATE the same presenter draws silence. The four states that refuse (`unconfirmed`, `withdrawn`, `incomplete`, `forked`) go to a presenter of an admitted face alone.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:114:''A route names its tier, and a tier names its root.'' A ''floor route'' answers at a locked vessel: the public shelf, the oracle's read face, the floor's announcement, and a herm's blind relay of bytes it cannot open. Its bundle derives from the floor key. A ''sovereign route'' seats a face's session, syncs a private document or serves a lane whose bytes this vessel can open. Its bundle derives from the sealed custody root, and it exists only while the vessel stands unlocked. A route's typed name carries its tier, the pin states it and the pin's digest binds it: no route asks the other tier's root, a root asked for the wrong tier refuses by name, and a dialer that pinned one tier believes no gate of the other.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:120:''What each tier costs.'' A thief who holds the disk and no passphrase holds the floor key: that thief can stand the floor gates, and can speak as the PLACE wherever the place's own key speaks (its carrier seal, a place arm), which reaches the public floor and the blind carriage of bytes it cannot open. That thief can never stand a sovereign gate, seat a face or open a sealed byte, and stands a serving gate only where the vessel's embers answer its copy (the serving tier, below).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:128:''A serving route answers at a vessel its embers raised to SERVING'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>): the serving gate for presenters already standing, and blind carriage for them. Its bundle derives from the serving key under its own registered domain, and it exists only while the vessel stands at SERVING or unlocked. The floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched: no serving route asks the floor key or the custody root, and a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier believes no serving gate. A serving gate signs its own handshake and no act, and its seat reaches what the serving tier holds and nothing beyond it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:238:| `forked` | two different events the face key signed stand at one position, or an event names a predecessor the gate's line never held | it refuses every certificate under that face key, keeps the events that prove it, and keeps counting every denial on every branch | nothing clears it but a face-key roll (#/causal-withdrawal) |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:243:''A gate's learned state only accretes.'' Learning reads as a union of verified events, whatever order they arrive in. An older frontier never replaces a later one, a denial once counted keeps counting through a fork and after it, and a fork once proven stays proven. A presentation that carries one event the gate cannot verify teaches the gate nothing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:245:''Only the face key can fork its history.'' A fork takes two events under the face key's own signature, so no vessel, relay or gate forges one, and a thief of one vessel's key gains no such power.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:249:''The vessel's own reading follows the same history.'' A vessel folds the events it receives against its own key: it reads //standing//, //withdrawn// or //forked//, and between a gate's ask and its own fold it reads `unconfirmed` and acts on nothing shared.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:363:* ''The floor and sovereign roots' doors'' stand at their seats (the serving key's door stands owed with train E), and no composer calls them until the socket cutover. A floor bundle asks the floor key's derive door (`vesselFloorKeyDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`), which answers while the vessel rests locked, hands back a fresh child its caller overwrites and never the floor key. A sovereign bundle asks the custody seat's (`custodyGateDoor`, `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-seat.ts`), which answers only while the seat holds its key. The two doors carry two types, so a line that hands one tier's door to the other fails to compile; a root refuses a door of the other tier and a door no mint made by name (`door-other-tier`); and each seat's door refuses the other tier's child by name. A door states only what its minter claimed, so one weld holds the minters to the two seats: a second caller of either mint, anywhere in source, turns it red (`packages/lararium-node/tests/gate-root-door-minters.test.ts`). The composer owes the call.
     1	/**
     2	 * place-floor-pin — a PLACE's floor pin, carried where a reader already holds the Nexus that carries the place, and the
     3	 * place's own presentation at that Nexus's floor gates.
     4	 *
     5	 * WHY A PLACE SIGNS ITS OWN PIN. A herm stands a floor gate only at a Nexus whose quorum counted a `carry` act over the
     6	 * herm's own vessel key (`placeCarriedNexuses`). Its floor pin derives from its floor key, which no seat holds, so no seat
     7	 * can mint it; and an announcement never authenticates its own first pin (house ruling "The admit's gate pin"). So the
     8	 * herm signs ONE statement per Nexus with the key the quorum's act names: `{ kind, placeKey, nexus, route, tier, digest }`
     9	 * over the pin it stands there. A reader files that pin only when
    10	 *
    11	 *   1. the statement reads whole, its pin reads whole, at floor tier, at the Nexus the reader asked, on the route asked;
    12	 *   2. the place's signature verifies under `placeKey`, over this exact image (domain-separated from every other seal);
    13	 *   3. the reader's OWN held root of that Nexus counts a `carry` for `placeKey` (the carrier fold over its own replica).
    14	 *
    15	 * The quorum's act authenticates the key; the key authenticates the pin. A statement for an uncarried key, a pin of
    16	 * another Nexus or route, or a torn signature files nothing. The statement rides the Nexus's carriage board beside the acts
    17	 * (a sidecar keyed by the place key, which the act extractor skips), so any replica writer may carry it and none can forge
    18	 * it (lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/place-floor-pin, whose status line names its standing).
    19	 *
    20	 * OWED (the carrier's #/owed): the statement carries no causal position, and the pair index holds no replace, so an older
    21	 * valid statement can stand in for a newer one after a floor-key rotation until the index drops it.
    22	 *
    23	 * THE PLACE ARM. A place presents the quorum's counted `carry` act over its own key at the gate's Nexus, with every
    24	 * counted act of that relation in its causal past as the lineage the gate's reader walks (`verifyPresentedCarry`). The
    25	 * head is the counted `carry` no other counted act of this place descends from; a counted `uncarry` that descends from it
    26	 * leaves the place with no arm to present.
    27	 *
    28	 * Meme: lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/place-floor-pin
    29	 */
